Test scope:
  Real source RDB + PSYNC -> local fsynced segments -> real cold pending apply.
  Five subtests: automatic reconnect/reopen, resource pause/resume,
  lost cold EXEC response/explicit recovery, unsupported TTL, real backlog gap.
  Source writes during stopped capture are real writes, not appended fixtures.
  Disk-low test injects available-byte samples; no actual filesystem exhaustion.
  Backlog test changes only this dedicated source's backlog size and restores it.
  No benchmark, throughput claim, power-cut test, production RPO or TTL support.

Pre-final validation and findings:
  Initial local runner race suite: PASS (3 repetitions, 8.700s).
  Initial whole gateway race: PASS (16.946s).
  Initial go test ./...: PASS; gateway 15.591s, server 54.305s.
  Initial go vet ./internal/gateway and git diff --check: PASS.

  Source cancellation review found that a prior blanket ctx.Err override could
  hide a concurrent journal/protocol failure. It was removed; deterministic
  tests retain corrupt/full/unsupported errors even when cancellation races.

  First real five-case run: PASS, 0.80s.
  Binary: /fixture/redis-pilot-g6-runner-e2e-20260908.test
  SHA256 local/remote: c20ae350601196e817a7178a7a2416c2569d85e0b5105e1bf59183ec809f0401
  Repeat count=3 on this binary: FAIL overall, one stop race in first repetition;
  remaining two repetitions and all other subtests passed.
  Actual failure:
    sync_runner_integration_test.go:208:
    read tcp 127.0.0.1:32912->127.0.0.1:6666: use of closed network connection
  Cause: cancel interrupted a cold read/validation and returned raw network
  error instead of context cancellation. This was a stop-result classification
  issue, not a counter mismatch. The chained segments regression did NOT run
  after this failed command. The failed binary is preserved, not overwritten.

  Correction: only raw network read/write/EOF cancellation is normalized at the
  runner drain boundary. Known terminal outcomes (especially uncertain EXEC)
  and unknown wrapped failures remain failures. No extra retry authority added.
  Added deterministic cancellation tests and direct DEL/SET cold assertions.

  Second pre-final binary: /fixture/redis-pilot-g6-runner-final-20260908.test
  SHA256 local/remote: 9b95f72e9f9f24537b7850077f629c780e54939bee58e9c9ce20aaffd0cc7f55
  Repeat count=10: FAIL overall, 9 complete repetitions passed; repetition 4
  correctly retained errSyncPendingUncertain when cancellation hit EXEC, but
  the test's stop assertion incorrectly required context.Canceled only.
  Actual failure: sync_runner_integration_test.go:189:
    pending sync outcome uncertain; reopen and reconcile pending record
  No production relaxation was made: immediate cancellation may interrupt a
  transaction and MUST retain this terminal result. The test now checks failed
  + cold_outcome_uncertain, then explicitly reconciles with a fresh bounded
  context, checks the exact expected counter and zero leaked views. Other stop
  errors still fail. Lost-response fault subtest still demands terminal failure
  before its separate explicit restart. This is not a silent auto-retry.

